1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,043
两位钟表匠。同样的手艺，同样一千个零件的表。
Two watchmakers. Same skill. Same thousand-part watch.

2
00:00:06,043 --> 00:00:11,195
一个越做越兴旺，另一个最后丢了铺子。为什么？
One prospered. The other lost his shop. Why?

3
00:00:11,895 --> 00:00:13,802
一切从一通电话开始。
It starts with a phone call.

4
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:16,763
电话一响，两人都得放下手里的活。
The phone rings, and both of them put their work down.

5
00:00:16,763 --> 00:00:19,570
一个回来，接着往下做。
One comes back and picks up where he left off.

6
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:22,306
另一个回来，面对的是一堆散落的零件。
The other comes back to a pile of loose parts.

7
00:00:22,306 --> 00:00:27,528
差别不在天赋，而在被打断之后，还剩下什么。
The difference isn't talent. It's what still stands after an interruption.

8
00:00:27,828 --> 00:00:30,076
他们一个叫霍拉（Hora），一个叫坦帕斯（Tempus）。
Their names were Hora and Tempus.

9
00:00:30,076 --> 00:00:33,661
两人做的都是好表，每块大约一千个零件。
Both made very fine watches, about a thousand parts each.

10
00:00:33,661 --> 00:00:36,926
两人都很抢手，电话整天响个不停。
Both were in demand, so their phones rang all day.

11
00:00:37,226 --> 00:00:40,717
坦帕斯一口气往下装，一个零件接一个零件。
Tempus built his watch in one long run, part after part.

12
00:00:40,717 --> 00:00:44,354
可半成品只要一放下，就立刻散架。
But if he had to put a half-finished watch down, it fell to pieces.

13
00:00:44,354 --> 00:00:48,886
装到第七百个，电话响了。归零。
Seven hundred parts in, the phone rings. Back to zero.

14
00:00:48,886 --> 00:00:52,344
顾客越喜欢他的表，打来的电话就越多，
And the more customers loved his watches, the more they called,

15
00:00:52,344 --> 00:00:56,192
他也就越难找到一段不被打断的时间，哪怕只做完一块。
and the harder it was to find enough quiet time to finish even one.

16
00:00:56,492 --> 00:01:01,546
霍拉的表一样复杂，但他的装法不同。
Hora's watches were just as complex. But he built them differently.

17
00:01:01,546 --> 00:01:06,066
他先把大约十个零件装成一个小组件，放下也不会散。
He joined about ten parts into a small subassembly that held together on its own.

18
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:11,002
十个小组件拼成一个大组件，十个大组件组成整块表。
Ten of those made a larger unit. Ten larger units made the watch.

19
00:01:11,002 --> 00:01:14,786
所以电话响时，他只丢掉手上正在装的那一小截。
So when his phone rang, he lost only the little piece in his hands.

20
00:01:14,786 --> 00:01:17,633
已经扣好的部分，都还在。
Everything already clicked together stayed together.

21
00:01:17,633 --> 00:01:22,247
同样一千个零件，霍拉多了一个站得住的中间层。
Same thousand parts. But Hora had a stable middle layer.

22
00:01:22,547 --> 00:01:27,467
这个寓言出自科学家赫伯特·西蒙 1962 年的一篇论文。
This parable comes from the scientist Herbert Simon, in a 1962 paper.

23
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:32,781
他还算了算差距有多大。不是去测量真实的钟表匠，
He also worked out how big the gap is. Not by measuring real watchmakers,

24
00:01:32,781 --> 00:01:34,875
而是做一个思想实验。
but as a thought experiment.

25
00:01:35,175 --> 00:01:39,716
假设每装上一个零件，电话响起的概率是百分之一。
Suppose that every time you add a part, there's a one-in-a-hundred chance the phone rings.

26
00:01:39,716 --> 00:01:42,316
那么，差距就落在三个数上。
Then the gap comes down to three numbers.

27
00:01:42,616 --> 00:01:45,634
第一个数：霍拉要装配的次数更多。
Number one: Hora has more assembling to do.

28
00:01:45,634 --> 00:01:49,606
一百个小组件，十个大组件，再加最后一次总装。
A hundred small units, ten larger ones, and one final watch.

29
00:01:49,606 --> 00:01:53,512
一共 111 次装配，而坦帕斯只装一次。
That's 111 assemblies, where Tempus does just one.

30
00:01:53,512 --> 00:01:56,188
单看这一项，坦帕斯占优。
On this count alone, Tempus is ahead.

31
00:01:56,488 --> 00:01:59,351
第二个数：一次打断，损失多少。
Number two: what one interruption costs.

32
00:01:59,351 --> 00:02:03,876
电话一响，坦帕斯平均丢掉大约 100 个零件的活。
When the phone rings, Tempus loses about 100 parts of work, on average.

33
00:02:03,876 --> 00:02:05,778
霍拉只丢大约 5 个。
Hora loses about 5.

34
00:02:05,778 --> 00:02:08,443
每次打断，损失相差 20 倍。
20 times more lost, every time.

35
00:02:08,743 --> 00:02:12,489
第三个数：一次装配不被打断、顺利做完的机会。
Number three: the chance of finishing one assembly without a call.

36
00:02:12,489 --> 00:02:20,708
霍拉只需连续装 10 个：0.99 的 10 次方，大约十次成九次。
For Hora, that's 10 parts in a row. 0.99 to the 10th power: about 9 times in 10.

37
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:29,620
坦帕斯要连续装 1000 个：0.99 的 1000 次方，一百万次里大约只成 44 次。
For Tempus, it's 1,000 in a row. 0.99 to the 1,000th power: about 44 chances in a million.

38
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:35,534
所以每做成一次装配，坦帕斯要尝试的次数，大约是霍拉的 20,000 倍。
So for each assembly he completes, Tempus needs about 20,000 times as many attempts as Hora.

39
00:02:35,834 --> 00:02:37,750
现在，把三项乘起来。
Now multiply the three.

40
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:44,148
111 分之一，乘以 20，再乘以 20,000。
1/111, times 20, times 20,000.

41
00:02:44,148 --> 00:02:45,910
大约 4,000。
Roughly 4,000.

42
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:50,210
两万倍（20,000），是每次装配的尝试次数之比。
20,000 is the ratio of attempts, per assembly.

43
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:54,088
四千倍（4,000），是做成一整块表的总时间之比。
4,000 is the ratio of total time, per finished watch.

44
00:02:54,388 --> 00:02:59,447
如果霍拉做一块表要一天，坦帕斯平均要大约 4,000 天。
If Hora needs one day for a watch, Tempus needs, on average, about 4,000 days.

45
00:02:59,447 --> 00:03:01,326
那是十年还不止。
That's more than ten years.

46
00:03:01,526 --> 00:03:07,837
不是因为他手慢，也不是他没耐心。只是因为电话响时，有些东西会散掉。
Not because he's slower, or less patient. Only because of what falls apart when the phone rings.

47
00:03:08,137 --> 00:03:12,705
西蒙给霍拉这种结构起了个名字：近似可分解系统。
Simon had a name for Hora's kind of structure: a nearly decomposable system.

48
00:03:12,705 --> 00:03:18,467
每个组件内部，零件扣得很紧；组件之间，连接很弱。
Inside each unit, the parts are tightly bound. Between units, the links are weak.

49
00:03:18,467 --> 00:03:22,766
弱，但不是可以忽略。这是他的原话。
Weak, but not negligible. Those are his words.

50
00:03:22,766 --> 00:03:26,819
在短时间里，几乎可以把每个组件单独来看。
Over a short stretch, you can look at each unit almost on its own.

51
00:03:26,819 --> 00:03:30,510
时间一长，那些弱连接仍在起作用。
Over a longer stretch, those weak connections still do their work.

52
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:38,827
西蒙还借这个寓言追问：复杂系统究竟是怎么形成的。那一部分，他自己也只当作推测。
Simon used this parable to ask a bigger question: how complex systems form at all. That part, he offered as speculation.

53
00:03:39,127 --> 00:03:40,791
回到那通电话。
Back to the phone call.

54
00:03:40,791 --> 00:03:45,585
你手上正在做的事，如果此刻电话响了，还剩下什么站得住？
Whatever you're building right now, if the phone rang this minute, what would still be standing?

55
00:03:45,585 --> 00:03:47,763
有没有一个放下也不会散的中间层？
Is there a middle layer that holds?

56
00:03:47,763 --> 00:03:52,683
还有那些你觉得弱到可以不管的连接，时间一长，会不会回来？
And the links you've written off as too weak to matter, given enough time, will they come back?

57
00:03:52,683 --> 00:03:54,272
电话又响了。
The phone is ringing.

